    <description>
      The Pioneer Venus Orbiter Turbulence Experiment (OTUR) used S- and
      X-band radio signals to measure turbulence intensity variations with
      altitude; planetary latitude and longitude; and atmospheric scale size
      distribution. It was designed to observe turbulence of scale sizes
      smaller than 10 km in the Venus atmosphere above 34 km for studying
      global patterns, and to measure ionospheric electron density variations.
    </description>
